color:color-mix(in_oklab,var(--accent-fill)_60%,var(--card))]"></rect><rect x="8" y="373" width="148" height="127" rx="11" data-with="team knowledge" style="animation-delay:0.39s" fill="none" stroke-width="2" class="ah-factory-flash stroke-[color:var(--factory-lit)]"></rect><g class="ah-factory-type"><text x="20" y="399" class="fill-foreground text-[16px] font-bold tracking-[-0.018em]">Knowledge</text><text class="fill-[color:var(--ah-fg-muted)] text-[13px]"><tspan x="20" y="418">Codebase design,</tspan><tspan x="20" y="435">testing,</tspan><tspan x="20" y="452">constraining code,</tspan><tspan x="20" y="469">good ol’ software</tspan><tspan x="20" y="486">fundamentals.</tspan></text></g></g><g data-node="accelerators" data-with="accelerators infrastructure agent"><rect x="180" y="174" width="148" height="127" rx="11" class="ah-factory-box fill-card stroke-[color:color-mix(in_oklab,var(--foreground)_14%,var(--card))]"></rect><rect x="180" y="174" width="148" height="127" rx="11" data-with="infrastructure accelerators" style="animation-delay:7.19s" fill="none" stroke-width="2" class="ah-factory-flash stroke-[color:var(--factory-lit)]"></rect><g class="ah-factory-type"><text x="192" y="200" class="fill-foreground text-[16px] font-bold tracking-[-0.018em]">Accelerators</text><text class="fill-[color:var(--ah-fg-muted)] text-[13px]"><tspan x="192" y="219">Schedules and</tspan><tspan x="192" y="236">triggers that initiate</tspan><tspan x="192" y="253">agents on their own,</tspan><tspan x="192" y="270">without human</tspan><tspan x="192" y="287">intervention.</tspan></text></g></g><g data-node="infrastructure" data-with="infrastructure team accelerators"><rect x="180" y="373" width="148" height="127" rx="11" class="ah-factory-box fill-card stroke-[color:color-mix(in_oklab,var(--foreground)_14%,var(--card))]"></rect><rect x="180" y="373" width="148" height="127" rx="11" data-with="team infrastructure" style="animation-delay:6.39s" fill="none" stroke-width="2" class="ah-factory-flash stroke-[color:var(--factory-lit)]"></rect><g class="ah-factory-type"><text x="192" y="399" class="fill-foreground text-[16px] font-bold tracking-[-0.018em]">Infrastructure</text><text class="fill-[color:var(--ah-fg-muted)] text-[13px]"><tspan x="192" y="418">Data sources,</tspan><tspan x="192" y="435">sandboxes and</tspan><tspan x="192" y="452">scripts that allow</tspan><tspan x="192" y="469">agents to work AFK.</tspan></text></g></g></svg></div><div class="sr-only"><p>Two paths run from the team to the agent. The Team builds Infrastructure, which creates Accelerators, which speed up The Agent. The Team grows Knowledge, which creates Brakes, which slow down The Agent.</p><dl><dt>The Agent</dt><dd>The model and harness building the code. The tactician.</dd><dt>The Team</dt><dd>The actual humans working on the codebase &amp; factory. The strategic thinkers.</dd><dt>Brakes</dt><dd>Automated checks, automated &amp; human review. Slows the agent down and increases quality.</dd><dt>Knowledge</dt><dd>Codebase design, testing, constraining code, good ol’ software fundamentals.</dd><dt>Accelerators</dt><dd>Schedules and triggers that initiate agents on their own, without human intervention.</dd><dt>Infrastructure</dt><dd>Data sources, sandboxes and scripts that allow agents to work AFK.</dd></dl></div></figure>
<p class="ah-prose-p">The goal of any software factory is <strong class="ah-prose-strong">speed</strong>. You and your team want to go fast. You want to delegate more work to the agent. And you want to get more done.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">So most folks start building <strong class="ah-prose-strong">accelerators</strong>. They start “loop engineering”, building systems that trigger work without human intervention. They start building <strong class="ah-prose-strong">infrastructure</strong> to connect their agents to data sources, and to run them in sandboxes.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">But speed without quality and control is how we end up with even more heaps of slop to clean up. That&#x27;s why starting with accelerators is backwards.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">Before you can trust your agent to go fast, you need to know that the quality of work is going to be high at any speed. You’ve gotta know how to use the brakes.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">And the best brakes are the ones we’ve always had: codebase design, testing, adding guardrails to code. Applying the knowledge our industry has developed over the last 50 years.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">In this cohort, we’ll spend <em class="ah-prose-em">a lot</em> of our time learning and building your Software Factory&#x27;s brakes.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">You will…</p>
<ol class="ah-numbers">
<li><strong class="ah-prose-strong">Learn how to create and document the knowledge</strong> needed to keep everybody on the same page: ubiquitous language, the project map, ADRs, specs and tickets, and ever-improving code.</li>
<li><strong class="ah-prose-strong">Create coding standards</strong>. From guidance through written instructions, to enforcement through tests, linters, type checks, automated review, and more.</li>
<li><strong class="ah-prose-strong">Build 3 layers of safety and sanity checks</strong>: automated checks, automated review, and human review (when your priorities call for it, with incredibly readable PRs).</li>
<li><strong class="ah-prose-strong">Make your codebase better than it&#x27;s ever been before.</strong> For you, your team, your users, and your coding agents, using the Software Factory you&#x27;ve engineered and built.</li>
</ol>
<p class="ah-prose-p">You&#x27;ll build a real, working Software Factory just like the one I work with every day, using a provided example code base (keeping your own codebase safe until you’re confident).</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">Then, you&#x27;ll practice designing your own for <em class="ah-prose-em">your</em> codebase, <em class="ah-prose-em">your</em> team and <em class="ah-prose-em">your</em> needs.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">And by the end, you’ll know how to develop your custom brakes and steering systems that support your engineering choices, preferences, and goals.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p"><strong class="ah-prose-strong">No more chasing bugs:</strong> your factory triages them for you.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p"><strong class="ah-prose-strong">No more babysitting:</strong> your agents report back when work is done, or when they need your input.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">And best of all, no more brain fry, so you can spend more of your precious brain juice thinking about building great software.</p>
