<h2 id="full-schedule-what-you-ll-be-learning-doing-and-building-each-week" class="scroll-mt-[72px] tracking-[-0.025em]"><a class="text-inherit! w-full font-semibold no-underline" href="#full-schedule-what-you-ll-be-learning-doing-and-building-each-week">Full Schedule: What you&#x27;ll be learning, doing, and building each week</a></h2>
<p class="ah-prose-p">On day one, you&#x27;ll get full access to all of the lessons, letting you pick your pace and schedule. Rip through lessons, or take your time; revisit to make sure you understand, and bring questions to Office Hours!</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">For the best experience, here&#x27;s my <em class="ah-prose-em">recommended</em> schedule that starts the moment you join, and continues through both weeks of the cohort:</p>
<h3 id="before-we-begin-ai-coding-crash-course-included-free" class="scroll-mt-[72px] tracking-[-0.025em]"><a class="text-inherit! w-full font-semibold no-underline" href="#before-we-begin-ai-coding-crash-course-included-free">Before We Begin: AI Coding Crash Course (Included Free)</a></h3>
<p class="ah-prose-p">To help you hit the ground running on Day 1, once you enroll you&#x27;ll get immediate access to my <a class="ah-prose-a" href="/workshops/ai-coding-crash-course">AI Coding Crash Course</a>.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">I launched this self-guided course over the summer to help folks get up to speed on the fundamentals of working with AI coding agents as quickly as possible: how AI models work, how coding harnesses work, and the importance of your agent’s environment.</p>
<div class="bg-linear-to-r bg-size-[200%_100%] animate-pulse from-gray-100 via-gray-200 to-gray-100 dark:from-gray-800 dark:via-gray-700 dark:to-gray-800 mx-auto my-8 w-full max-w-md rounded-md" style="aspect-ratio:480 / 600;max-width:480px;max-height:600px;width:100%;height:auto"></div>
<p class="ah-prose-p"><strong class="ah-prose-strong">Even if you’re already using AI coding agents every day, you do not want to skip this Crash Course!</strong> Treat it as a prerequisite for getting the most out of the cohort itself.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">You can complete the Crash Course end to end in roughly three days, or use it as reference material to fill in the gaps you need the most.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">The lessons and exercises inside will make sure you have all of the knowledge and understanding to build your own Software Factory.</p>
<div role="separator" class="ah-divider"></div>
<h3 id="week-1-from-domain-language-to-codebase-design" class="scroll-mt-[72px] tracking-[-0.025em]"><a class="text-inherit! w-full font-semibold no-underline" href="#week-1-from-domain-language-to-codebase-design">Week 1: From Domain Language to Codebase Design</a></h3>
<p class="ah-prose-p">Kick off the cohort with a live Office Hours, giving you a chance to ask me your burning questions <em class="ah-prose-em">before</em> you begin.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">Then jump right in by getting you and your agent speaking the same language. You&#x27;ll build a shared glossary and write ADRs with <code class="ah-code-inline">/grill-with-docs</code>, so your agents (and your teammates) stop misunderstanding what you mean.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">Next, learn to plan work far too big for one agent session. With the Wayfinder skill, you&#x27;ll chart a map of the work, grill and prototype the risky parts, and turn it into specs your factory can build.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">After that, focus on the best ways to create and use the brakes that will keep your agent in your control. You&#x27;ll learn the three kinds of review, how to make human review faster and how to prioritize it, and how to run a retro that improves the system that wrote the code, not just the code itself.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">Finally, we&#x27;ll finish the week with codebase design. You&#x27;ll learn what makes a codebase easy for agents to work in, from deep modules and enforced boundaries to rescuing legacy code and making it testable.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">By the end of the first week, you&#x27;ll be able to plan huge chunks of work, trust what comes back, and shape a codebase your agents can find their way around.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p"><strong class="ah-prose-strong">We&#x27;ll wrap up Week 1 with Office Hours.</strong> Bring your questions, get direct answers. Can&#x27;t make it live? Submit your question in advance and get the recording and transcript.</p>
<div role="separator" class="ah-divider"></div>
<h3 id="week-2-feedback-loops-and-building-your-factory" class="scroll-mt-[72px] tracking-[-0.025em]"><a class="text-inherit! w-full font-semibold no-underline" href="#week-2-feedback-loops-and-building-your-factory">Week 2: Feedback Loops and Building Your Factory</a></h3>
<p class="ah-prose-p">Week 2 stacks on top of everything you learn in Week 1, introducing the automation that keeps a Software Factory safe and trustworthy at any speed.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">First, you&#x27;ll make bad code (nearly) impossible, with automated checks, custom lint rules, mutation testing and verification for frontend apps.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">Then for the rest of the week, you&#x27;ll put it all together and build a Software Factory like mine.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">You’ll learn how I use GitHub Actions to automatically investigate, triage, assign, delegate, track and review units of work. And finally, you&#x27;ll practice designing your own for your codebase and your team.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p"><strong class="ah-prose-strong">Week 2 Office Hours with Matt.</strong> Same format, deeper questions. By now you&#x27;ll have real experience to draw from, so we can help you connect the dots between your practice and real work in your codebase!</p>
<div role="separator" class="ah-divider"></div>
<h3 id="works-with-your-favorite-harness-or-model" class="scroll-mt-[72px] tracking-[-0.025em]"><a class="text-inherit! w-full font-semibold no-underline" href="#works-with-your-favorite-harness-or-model">Works with your favorite harness or model</a></h3>
<p class="ah-prose-p">This course focuses on the Claude Code CLI, which is where I&#x27;ve honed these skills and gotten the best results myself. So it&#x27;s the best way for me to teach you!</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">But once you&#x27;ve practiced the skills here, you&#x27;ll be able to use the same techniques and knowledge in just about any CLI coding assistant, with virtually any frontier AI model.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">And the more you practice these skills, the more powerful your software factory can become.</p>
<h3 id="learn-on-your-schedule-from-anywhere" class="scroll-mt-[72px] tracking-[-0.025em]"><a class="text-inherit! w-full font-semibold no-underline" href="#learn-on-your-schedule-from-anywhere">Learn on your schedule, from anywhere</a></h3>
